The published image is the official PostgreSQL Docker image (docker.io/library/postgres:18-alpine),
unmodified, with pgvector added:

- PostgreSQL, distributed under the PostgreSQL License. https://www.postgresql.org/about/licence/
- pgvector (https://github.com/pgvector/pgvector), distributed under the PostgreSQL License. Its
  license ships in the image at /usr/local/share/licenses/pgvector/LICENSE.

The base image's Alpine packages keep their own licenses; the image's BuildKit SBOM lists them.
